WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.480
Enter the fray, king of all knights!

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.230
Ride, the King of Knights, Alfred!

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.580
And I call Blaster Blade to the rear-guard!

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.980
Final turn.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.040
Hey, it's not over yet!

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.380
I used up my hand, but I 
wasn't able to defend them all...

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.630
Toshiki Kai vs. Misaki Tokura!

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.190
The winner is Kai!

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.820
Kai won.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.280
Kai...

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.450
That was a good fight, Kai.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.130
My victory was guaranteed.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.600
All right...

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.620
I can fight Kai if I win this fight.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.900
I'm gonna win, for sure!

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.370
Brother Aichi's really fired up.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.320
But Miss Emi's also watching.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.960
I can't lose, either!

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.990
It's my turn to attack.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.960
If I can give him 2 damage...

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.080
I've got to get my attacks through, somehow!

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:49.990
Here we go, full power!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:55.420
The End of the Shop Tournament

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.570
I switch the places of Marron and Epona.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.890
And I call Gancelot here!

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.350
I call Wingal, as well.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.840
He's changing his battle formation 
to increase attack power, I see...

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.580
But this is the crucial moment for me, too.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.440
I'm going to defend with everything I've got.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.870
I power up Blaster Blade 
by boosting with Wingal!

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.790
I attack the Vanguard Mr. Invincible!

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.320
Plus, using Wingal's skill, power +4000!

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.520
I'll let it through.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.300
But that one's really easy to guard!

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.170
RG, yo!

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.510
Damage trigger check.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.980
Got a trigger!

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:48.170
I give power +5000 to my Vanguard Invincible!

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.500
Plus, I stand my rear-guard Invincible!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.850
I attack your Vanguard 
Invincible with Alfred!

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.310
Royal Paladin brethren, 
give Alfred your power!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.510
I guard with Shining Lady!

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.240
A shield of 10000... Combine that with 
Invincible's 15000 and you get 25000.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.810
Alfred's 20000, so that defense will hold.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.610
I guard with Rock the Wall!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.450
Hey... He's already defended plenty, right?

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.640
All that's doing is wasting his hand...

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.350
No, there's no way to tell yet.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.110
Twin drive!

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.350
First check.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.400
Second check.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.560
Critical trigger, activate!

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:46.010
But even with a power of 25000, 
the attack won't get through...

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.910
What the...

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.990
Even though he got a trigger, and 
could increase his attack power...

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:57.580
Kamui used two cards to guard, 
thinking about just this possibility.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.700
But this trigger won't be in vain!

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.340
Critical trigger, activate!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.140
I add +5000 power and +1 damage to Gancelot!

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.980
Gancelot is the only card left 
who can attack this turn.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.860
I'll bet everything on this attack!

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:19.310
Shining Lady goes to the drop zone.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.810
Using Rock the Wall's skill,

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.120
after it finishes guarding, 
it moves to the Soul.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.250
That makes five cards in the Soul.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:30.130
I attack your Vanguard with 
Gancelot, boosted by Marron!

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:33.540
How about that?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.110
He's only got two cards in his hand...

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.500
Does he have a card left he can guard with?

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:40.940
I guard with Rock the Wall!

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.260
I move Rock the Wall to the Soul.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:57.900
I gave it all I had, but I only 
got a single attack through...

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.100
If only I could have gotten 1 more damage!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:04.060
Hey... About that Rock the Wall...

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.750
Doesn't it usually go to the drop 
zone after it guards, like a normal card?

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.490
That card's special.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:13.450
You can place it in the Soul 
instead of the drop zone.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.590
Oh?

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:18.120
Now that you mention it, 
Kamui's Soul's pretty big now.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.210
I stand and draw!

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:25.090
Now, Brother... I'll 
finish it with this turn!

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.300
I can't let him do that.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.300
I'll defend to the end, you'll see!

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.400
Here I go!

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.810
Ride, from Invincible to Invincible!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:36.510
Huh?

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:40.570
Huh?

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:42.390
Why would he ride another Invincible?

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.400
What's the point of that Ride?

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:51.110
And I Soulcharge using Invincible's skill!

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.930
That makes eight cards in my Soul.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:59.410
But, unless I get a card that lets me turn cards 
back over in my damage zone, I can't activate it.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:02.760
Is he increasing his Soul 
without it doing anything?

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.500
I call King of Sword!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.630
Now, I end this!

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.510
I attack Alfred with the King of Sword!

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:16.390
Should I let this through?

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.270
Damage trigger check...

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.340
He still has two more attacks.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.380
If I can defend against 
them, this isn't over yet!

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.580
I boost with Shining Lady, and attack Alfred!

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.320
Go, Invincible!

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:36.660
I guard!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.410
Llew, please!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:49.090
Okay! Next is the final attack.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.900
I boost with Lucky Girl,

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.470
and attack Alfred with Invincible!

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:57.720
I guard with Morgana!

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.900
Plus, I intercept with Blaster Blade!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.090
Twin drive!

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:07.310
First check.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:10.600
If he doesn't get a drive 
trigger, then I'll make it!

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.760
Second check!

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.820
Stand trigger!

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.100
I stand King of Sword!

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:22.540
Plus, I add +5000 power to this Invincible!

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.790
I guess this is it?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.880
Iron Fist Strike!

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.430
Damage trigger check...

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.260
I got a heal trigger!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:42.260
I use its effect to raise 
Alfred's power +5000!

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.970
And I recover 1 damage.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.390
Attacks are over...

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.800
I defended, somehow or another...

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:53.620
Not so fast, Brother.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:57.740
Mr. Invincible, Soulblast...

00:09:58.190 --> 00:09:59.630
Say what?!

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.750
Soulblast!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.300
Say what?!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.780
I move eight cards from 
my Soul to the drop zone.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:21.350
And with a cost of 5, Counterblast!

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:26.480
With Mr. Invincible's 
skill, I stand all units!

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:41.950
This is his secret technique, 
Tornado Stand Galactica!

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.780
That power of Mr. Invincible's

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:59.010
requires eight Soul, and 
five unflipped damage.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:04.010
Plus, it can only be used 
after an attack hits.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:09.010
I see! So the reason he increased 
his Soul this turn was for this!

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.950
Oh! Now that you mention it...

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.840
Kamui's been preparing 
for this the whole time.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.110
Exciting!

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:21.370
All his units are now standing?

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.370
Here I come, Brother.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.700
This is the power of my Nova Grappler deck!

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.080
I boost with Lucky Girl,

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:32.050
and attack Alfred with Invincible!

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.720
I can't do anything...

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.770
Twin drive, first check!

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.350
Second check!

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:59.330
Iron Fist Strike!

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.250
Damage trigger check...

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.810
I've lost.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.270
Kai... I still can't fight you...

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.030
The first semi-final fight...

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:25.590
Winner: Kamui Katsuragi!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:29.940
Aichi...

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:33.280
I don't really get it, but...

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.010
But it was really exciting.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.940
Um... Nice fight!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.810
Uh, thanks, Emi.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:41.110
That's right.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.970
Morikawa, Izaki...

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.600
Well, you tried your best.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.550
Yeah! Not bad for someone like you, Aichi.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.850
Brother Aichi!

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:53.260
Honestly, you've gotten much 
better at Vanguard fights.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:56.110
You shouldn't feel bad for losing to me.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:58.580
That's right! The Great Kamui 
is the strongest, after all!

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.080
KS, yo!

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.210
Kamui...

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.160
Why you... Just rub it in, why don't you?

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.060
That's not what he's doing, Morikawa.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:09.230
Kamui's just worried 
about me, in his own way.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:12.020
My fight with you was a lot of fun, Kamui.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:16.060
It was fun... But...

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.980
Losing really does hurt, you know?

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:22.560
Aichi...

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:25.060
Yes.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:30.110
Kamui, we'll have the finals after 
a 10 minute break, so get ready.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:31.060
Roger that!

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:32.860
Miss Emi, watch me!

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.750
I'm gonna win it all, you'll see!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.110
Um...

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.500
It wasn't even close, Kamui the Great!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.750
Well, ya know...

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:46.460
Kamui?!

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:47.820
You okay?

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.390
I-It's nothing!

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:54.720
That's odd... Why are my knees rattling? 
It's like these aren't my own legs...

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:59.390
Kamui was really nervous too, I see.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.550
Did you have fun, Misaki?

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:22.180
Not really. Since I was 
forced to participate.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:33.740
I figure the winner will 
be that high-schooler, Kai.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.930
No way! It's gonna be the 
strongest grade-schooler, Kamui!

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.850
Wait a little longer, please.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.920
I'm sure something good awaits.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:41.480
Huh?

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:47.490
Okay, for the finals, let's use this 
Standing Fight Table(name subject to change) here!

00:14:56.840 --> 00:15:00.260
Manager, why is he looking down at me?!

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.600
Make my platform a little higher, sheesh!

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:06.270
But if I make it higher, you'll 
have trouble handling the cards.

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:09.040
You should give up raising 
another step, I think...

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.410
GU, yo...

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.720
Fine, too bad, then.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.730
This just doesn't feel right.

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.530
Aichi...

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.690
Now then...

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:26.740
It's what you've all been waiting for! 
The final fight of the Shop Tournament!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:28.350
Toshiki Kai vs.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.700
Kamui Katsuragi!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:33.520
I've been waiting for this!

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:34.930
I'm gonna...

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:35.490
...re-...

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.460
...reform you!

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:41.090
It's revenge! Reform what exactly?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.140
It's too bad you're my opponent.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.670
W-What?

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:51.720
I wanted to fight someone worthy in 
the finals. Someone I didn't know.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.300
Why, you...

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.100
Hey, what're you blanking out for?

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:58.240
Huh?

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:01.230
You still haven't gotten over it?

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:06.080
You know, when a rank-and-file gets 
trampled, they spring back even stronger!

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.370
That's grass!

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:08.610
Same dif!

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:12.010
Morikawa... Izaki...

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.200
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.540
Stand up... the Vanguard!

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:17.010
It's starting!

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:18.980
Time to watch!

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:20.200
S-Sure...

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:22.360
I ride Jarran.

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:23.800
I call Aermo.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.310
I ride Tough Boy!

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:34.580
Genocide Jack, rev up to full speed!

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.060
I attack with Genocide Jack!

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:42.560
I guard with the Lizard Soldier, Ganlu.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.980
The two of them are amazing...

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:57.870
Superior ride the Vanguard!

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.050
The Embodiment of Victory, Aleph!

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:06.210
Stand up and pay heed, all my warriors!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.580
Tornado Stand Galactica!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.480
That's the same skill I lost to!

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:22.220
Now I can attack three more times!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.890
Try me.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:24.930
What?

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.440
Don't mind if I do!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.020
I boost with Tough Boy,

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:32.600
and attack Dragonic Overlord 
with Clay-doll Mechanic!

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:37.990
Check the damage trigger.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:42.050
I boost with Clara, and 
attack with Mr. Invincible!

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:44.310
I guard with the Embodiment 
of the Spear, Tahr.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.010
He defended against two attacks!

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:51.190
There's still more! I boost with 
Shout, and attack with Tough Boy!

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.250
I intercept with Nehalem.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:59.110
Thanks to his attacks so far, too many of 
my rear-guard and hand have been used up!

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:01.350
My unit's power just isn't enough!

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.990
He's managed to defend against 
Kamui's attack, even with 5 damage.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.990
That's Kai for you.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:10.920
But Kamui is amazing as well.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.320
I can't believe he's backed 
Kai this far against the wall!

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:15.410
It's over now.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.700
Final turn!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.200
I knew it, those two are amazing...

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:28.080
Just watching the two fight like 
this... I can't hold in my excitement!

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:33.810
I boost with Bahr,

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:37.490
and attack Invincible with Dragonic Overlord!

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.780
I guard with Lucky Girl!

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:47.160
Twin drive.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.440
First check.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.900
Second check.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:58.240
I got a critical trigger.

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:02.030
I add +5000 power to Dragonic Overlord.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:06.370
Also, I add +1 to the damage that it gives.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.030
Damage trigger check...

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.600
The end.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.500
The winner of the Card 
Capital Shop Tournament is:

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:40.240
Toshiki Kai!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:46.080
Wow...

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:50.330
Both of them really are amazing fighters.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.070
One day, I want to be like them!

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.790
Yes, yes...

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:01.300
Now, since we've decided the 
winner of the Shop Tournament,

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.490
I have a very important announcement to make!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.980
Coming through...

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:08.100
The winner of the tournament today,

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.030
Toshiki Kai.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:12.550
The runner-up, Kamui Katsuragi.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:16.580
And the rest of the best four, 
Aichi Sendou and Misaki Tokura...

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.470
The four top finishers will enter here.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:22.750
There was a bigger poster, actually...

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:25.030
But the sub-manager kinda destroyed it...

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.120
Oh!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.460
Whoa!

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:28.710
Great going, Aichi!

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:29.990
What is it?

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:31.720
Whoa! Fantastic!

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:36.000
Misaki Tokura! It's the championships! 
A really big tournament!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:36.540
Huh?

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:40.820
These championships are the biggest 
Vanguard tournaments in all Japan!

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:45.300
You four will be the representatives 
sent from Card Capital!

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:50.390
First, you'll enter the regional 
tournament, and if you win that...

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:54.220
At the next national tournament, you'll 
battle with the best from around the country!

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:58.900
Whoever wins there will truly
 be the Best Fighters in Japan!

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:03.900
Although the teams consist of three people, 
so one of you will need to serve as a backup...

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:08.940
But you've all earned the honor of being 
worthy to participate in this tournament.

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:12.740
Everyone, please give these four 
a great big round of applause!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.090
Kamui, you're so great!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:19.930
Awesome!

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:21.080
You guys rock!

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.910
Wow, Aichi!

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:26.750
Brother Aichi!

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.440
Rejoice, man!

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.910
These are the championships I've dreamed of!

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:35.540
Me and my brother are gonna 
make our grand debut!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:40.070
All right! I can't wait! 
Show me what you've caught!

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.560
What you've caught?

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.130
He means "got"...

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:44.750
Miss Emi, please watch me!

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:45.330
Huh?

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:49.670
This time for sure, I'll win the regionals, 
and earn my place in the nationals...

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:51.240
And then, you and I will get...

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.640
M-M-M-M...

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:56.000
Let's do this!

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.980
I'm all fired up!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:02.230
I-I...

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:06.030
I'll be fighting alongside 
Kamui, Misaki, and Kai?

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:09.310
In the Vanguard Championships?

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.050
H-Huh?

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:15.490
Maybe this isn't the right picture...

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.410
Huh?

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:53.740
Participate in a regional 
Vanguard tournament?

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:58.420
Yup. The winner Kai, the runner-up 
Kamui, plus you and Misaki as well.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:23:59.440
Make me proud!

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:00.100
Right!

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:02.460
There's a bit of time before 
the regionals, though...

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:03.610
Prepare yourself.

00:24:03.610 --> 00:24:04.080
Right!

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:07.520
That's right... I want to 
become stronger, but how?

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:10.950
Next time: The Fearsome 
Undead! A Granblue Deck!

00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:12.920
This person is really strong!

00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:15.000
Oh, to another shop...

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:17.220
I guess the idea is to 
travel around training?

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:18.610
...to other shops...
